<source id="1" url="https://chat.codercops.com/core/providers/" title="AI Providers" section="OpenAI-compatible servers">
AI Providers > OpenAI-compatible servers

Any server that speaks the OpenAI chat completions API works through the `openai-compatible` provider. `baseURL` and `model` are required, `apiKey` only if the server wants one:

```typescript
import type { ProviderConfig } from '@chatcops/core';

const providers = {
  // Ollama on your own machine
  ollama: {
    type: 'openai-compatible',
    model: 'llama3.3',
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:11434/v1',
  },

  // OpenRouter, with the headers it uses to identify your app
  openrouter: {
    type: 'openai-compatible',
    apiKey: process.env.OPENROUTER_API_KEY!,
    model: 'anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5',
    baseURL: 'https://openrouter.ai/api/v1',
    headers: { 'HTTP-Referer': 'https://example.com', 'X-Title': 'My site' },
  },

  // A model that can't call tools
  withoutTools: {
    type: 'openai-compatible',
    model: 'gemma3',
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:11434/v1',
    supportsTools: false,
  },
} satisfies Record<string, ProviderConfig>;
```

`openai-compatible` sends `max_tokens`. If the server wants `max_completion_tokens`, set `maxTokensParam: 'max_completion_tokens'`.
</source>
