<source id="3" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/ai-sdk/" title="AI SDK (useChat)">
AI SDK (useChat)

`chatcopsAiSdkHandler` answers in the [AI SDK](https://ai-sdk.dev)'s UI message stream, so an app that already uses `useChat` can use a ChatCops server instead of its own route. You keep your chat UI and get ChatCops on the server: stored conversations, rate limits, budgets, allowed origins and tools.

It's a Fetch API handler like `chatcopsVercelHandler`, so it works as a Next.js route handler and in any runtime from the [fetch runtimes page](/server/fetch-runtimes/). It's tested against `ai` 7.
</source>
<source id="4" url="https://chat.codercops.com/core/providers/" title="AI Providers" section="Provider configuration">
AI Providers > Provider configuration

```typescript
import type { ProviderConfig } from '@chatcops/core';

const providers = {
  // Claude (Anthropic)
  claude: {
    type: 'claude',
    apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY!,
    model: 'claude-haiku-5-5', // Default
  },
  // OpenAI
  openai: {
    type: 'openai',
    apiKey: process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY!,
    model: 'gpt-5-mini', // Default
  },
  // Google Gemini
  gemini: {
    type: 'gemini',
    apiKey: process.env.GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY!,
    model: 'gemini-3.5-flash-lite', // Default
  },
  // Any OpenAI-compatible server
  compatible: {
    type: 'openai-compatible',
    baseURL: 'http://localhost:11434/v1',
    model: 'llama3.3',
  },
} satisfies Record<string, ProviderConfig>;
```

`apiKey` is required for `claude`, `openai` and `gemini`. Without it, setup fails with an error like `claude requires apiKey`.
</source>
