<source id="5" url="https://chat.codercops.com/getting-started/quick-start/" title="Quick Start" section="2. Set Up the Server">
Quick Start > 2. Set Up the Server

Install the server package:

```bash
npm install @chatcops/server express
```

Make a secret for the session tokens the widget fetches before it chats, and keep it with your API key (never in client code):

```bash
openssl rand -base64 32   # put it in CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET
```

Create a minimal Express server:

```typescript
import express from 'express';
import { chatcopsMiddleware } from '@chatcops/server';

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

// app.use, so /chat/session, where the widget gets its token, reaches it too.
app.use('/chat', chatcopsMiddleware({
  provider: {
    type: 'claude',
    apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY!,
    model: 'claude-haiku-5-5',
  },
  systemPrompt: `You are a helpful customer support assistant for our website.
    Be friendly, concise, and helpful.`,
  allowedOrigins: ['*'],
  sessionSecrets: [process.env.CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET!],
  rateLimit: { maxRequests: 30, windowMs: 60_000 },
}));

app.listen(3001, () => {
  console.log('ChatCops server running on http://localhost:3001');
});
```

Without `sessionSecrets` the server refuses to start, so a chat can't be left open by accident. To try it without one, set `allowAnonymous: true` instead. See [Session tokens](/server/setup/#session-tokens).
