<source id="3" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/security/" title="Security" section="A production config &gt; Cloudflare Workers">
Security > A production config > Cloudflare Workers

```typescript
import { chatcopsCloudflareHandler } from '@chatcops/server';
import { redisStorage } from '@chatcops/store-redis';
import { Redis } from '@upstash/redis/cloudflare';

let chat: ReturnType<typeof chatcopsCloudflareHandler> | undefined;

export default {
  fetch(request: Request, env: Env, ctx: ExecutionContext) {
    // Secrets only exist inside a request, so build the handler on the first one.
    chat ??= chatcopsCloudflareHandler({
      provider: { type: 'claude', apiKey: env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY },
      systemPrompt: 'You are the Acme support assistant.',
      storage: redisStorage({ redis: Redis.fromEnv(env) }),
      allowedOrigins: ['https://acme.com'],
      sessionSecrets: [env.CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET],
      turnstile: { secretKey: env.TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY },
      budgets: { globalPerDay: { tokens: 20_000_000 } },
    });
    return chat(request, env, ctx);
  },
};
```

The Worker gets every path, so `/session` needs nothing extra. The visitor's IP comes from `CF-Connecting-IP`.
</source>
<source id="4" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/cloudflare/" title="Cloudflare Workers Adapter" section="Setup">
Cloudflare Workers Adapter > Setup

Create a Worker at `src/index.ts`:

```typescript
import { chatcopsCloudflareHandler } from '@chatcops/server';

// Built on the first request rather than at import, because the API key is a
// Worker secret that only exists inside a request. Caching the handler here is
// what keeps conversation history and rate limiting alive across requests.
let handler: ReturnType<typeof chatcopsCloudflareHandler> | undefined;
function getHandler(env: Record<string, string>) {
  handler ??= chatcopsCloudflareHandler({
    provider: {
      type: 'claude',
      apiKey: env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
    },
    systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful assistant.',
    allowedOrigins: ['*'],
    // Signs the session tokens the widget gets from /session (a Worker sees every path).
    sessionSecrets: [env.CHATCOPS_SESSION_SECRET],
  });
  return handler;
}

export default {
  async fetch(
    request: Request,
    env: Record<string, string>
  ): Promise<Response> {
    return getHandler(env)(request);
  },
};
```

:::note[History and rate limits]
Conversation history and rate limiting live in memory on the isolate, not in a
shared store. They are not shared between isolates and they do not survive a
restart, so a deploy or a scale event resets both.
:::
</source>
